{"title":"2021 China National High School Mathematics League A1/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_China_National_High_School_Mathematics_League_A1/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> satisfy the following condition:\n</p><p>There exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b0390586049c40ec59f20639b2ab3ed69e7ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in[0,x], b\\in[0,y]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d0c54689a2881648e0144a3cb66f85bd3a8de1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+y^2=2, b^2+x^2=1, ax+by=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFind the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Trigonometric_Substitution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Trigonometric_Substitution)\">Solution 1 (Trigonometric Substitution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_China_National_High_School_Mathematics_League_A1/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Trigonometric Substitution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nSince the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4bad2b0d3d3b355c505923d17ed6e37060035de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2+x^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> is similar to that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1acaf0ddabcf2161f7b309ce5b107f667c7bbe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(m)+\\cos^2(m)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"22\" />, trying trigonometric substitution might be a useful way to boil down the variables. \n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b65204527c58013d9746fa25056972edaea41b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\sin(m), b=\\cos(m), a=\\sqrt{2}\\sin(n), y=\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"419\" height=\"24\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are degrees in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/2206ec333c5c3abbbe550b8d39d5aba8024ef371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,90^{\\circ}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, all real numbers in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e861e10e1c19918756b9c8b7717684593c63aeb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> varies.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, all real numbers in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a3c20c9b07b4629c161d739be6e6ab5a245461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\sqrt{2}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"24\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> varies. \n</p><p>The two equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f072eef7eb18423809842c5a36af865a01e5c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+y^2=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4bad2b0d3d3b355c505923d17ed6e37060035de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2+x^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> are automatically satisfied. We have shrunk the number of variables from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548b4593bc88cee312797a1016548c2a698ccf5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> is now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4af0a7ad31fe1d70b355d572198b30191651bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}\\sin(m)\\sin(n)+\\sqrt{2}\\cos(m)\\cos(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"322\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d8338ccd9f40ef0ccd7daf322533301df8e438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(m)\\sin(n)+\\cos(m)\\cos(n)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"286\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Apply the Difference of Angles formula.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0006b500c3dec098dec1e21071fc09e19894ab12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(m-n)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83dc9fb7fb140400bc420601048358222e0326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n=\\pm{45^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>The last step is correct because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/2206ec333c5c3abbbe550b8d39d5aba8024ef371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,90^{\\circ}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"20\" />. The difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f856886c87eb11dfe963fc0f61eafbe3d11e33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-90^{\\circ},90^{\\circ}]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e83dc9fb7fb140400bc420601048358222e0326e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n=\\pm{45^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> are the only two solutions in this range.\n</p><p><br />\nAs only one variable remains, we can finally calculate the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71e346bf0e9ad355e31aeaaeb32c098114a57803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)+\\sin(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b9f6e9babd6e075188c6417c8aca511b8abb40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)+\\sin(n\\pm{45^{\\circ}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"263\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p>Apply the Sum/Difference of Angles formula.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa83e6a95eaef40afb27840b3ac512553181ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)+\\sin(n)\\cos(45^{\\circ})\\pm\\cos(n)\\sin(45^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"419\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/8245c9e5ce85051bf4bc8f6f8f2bcab6c065c2cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin(n)\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"349\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/4/e640b2b8419cb59664913f97a4dc117ad7cf9186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is non-negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc67360097d2b5ac8403497506affdd867162cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"43\" /> is always greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b07a2f7073331835e4637e6885daabf06a0786.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"43\" />. We take the positive sign to obtain the upper bound of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbae12b71e5d0b97311a19f1564fbdb0fbffa0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y\\leq\\sqrt{2}\\cos(n)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin(n)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"349\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c305f2dd27c9bd1c3409b0ae25e734ac04494804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y\\leq\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos(n)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"259\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> to make the expression suitable for applying the Sum of Angles formula.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76fe353f1c3273ea7a1ed67ece9606b198788695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y\\leq\\sqrt{5}(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cos(n)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\sin(n))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"306\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the squares of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503c53d5f255300e8a0a4b5d2449bca61354ee41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"39\" height=\"48\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42ccd4efe537aec48f0733a0bd8c92846bd2642e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"39\" height=\"48\" /> is now exactly equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By the Sum of Angles formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/521803ff086feba45d62f0d7e3347e424df9a039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y\\leq\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBy manually calculating the equality case, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/4/b74c30cda19ca251dfe60523890f10d909c82755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}, b=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}, a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}, y=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"292\" height=\"43\" /> satisfy all the conditions simultaneously.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> is the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3da9f8c7fe0473fdd6f8597eff61d71fedda430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_China_National_High_School_Mathematics_League_A1/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The conditions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d7f0506b4ee793dbd65cd6c9151787349ef78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\leq{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1bef2f2950348bb4f6d4b1d1e141bcb088af08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\leq{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are completely useless in this problem. These two conditions never appeared in the proof, meaning that not a single step would need to change if these two conditions were removed.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153722\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 289/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10825/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36583:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153722 and revision id 282386. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}